CATEGORIES:Tradition & Community
CATEGORIES:Engage & Thrive - Community
CATEGORIES:Campus-Wide Event
DESCRIPTION:How do global political labels impact our national/local commu
 nities during election season\, and vice versa? This month\, WAAPI explor
 es the "Mamdani effect"\, a particular case of how the political categori
 zation of cultural and religious identities shapes public perception. We'
 ll discuss "representation": while Mamdani gives important visibility to 
 South Asian and Muslim voices\, that same spotlight has unfortunately led
  to a rise in Islamophobia and anti-Asian hate. We will also look at "exp
 ectations": while many South Asians are known for working in tech\, busin
 ess\, or medicine\, Mamdani breaks that mold as a youthful politician. Jo
 in us for an open\, student-led conversation. Free lunch is provided\, an
 d all students are welcome! \nWAAPI is a monthly roundtable discussion by
  and for students interested in learning and discussing issues impacting 
 the Asian American and Pacific Islander (AAPIs) and the general community
 . Lunch provided!  Free and open to all students.\n \nAll Indiana Univers
 ity events\, groups\, activities\, and educational\, cultural\, and histo
 rical observances welcome all IU students and other members of the Indian
 a University community.\n\nHosted by: Asian Culture Center\n\nAdditional 
 Information can be found at: https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/1247451
 8
DTEND:20261016T170000Z
DTSTAMP:20261010T053119Z
DTSTART:20261016T160000Z
LOCATION:Asian Culture Center (807 E 10th street\, Bloomington\, IN)
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY: Who are Asian Americans and Pacific Islanders? (WAAPI) A Lunch Di
 scussion On “[GI5.1][GI5.2]The Mamdani Effect & The Midterms”
UID:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12474518
URL:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12474518
X-HOSTS:Asian Culture Center
END:VEVENT
