DESCRIPTION:Who taught you that you had to work twice as hard to get half 
 as far?\nIf you’re always the one who says yes\, pushes through\, stays s
 trong\, or carries expectations from family\, community\, or campus\, thi
 s conversation is for you. Join us for “Twice as Hard”\, as we unpack the
  hidden pressures behind overworking\, redefine the difference between re
 st and laziness\, and explore the costs of carrying what was assigned to 
 you instead of chosen by you.\nYou don’t have to explain your experience 
 here. We’ll already understand. And\, we'll have light refreshments\n\nHo
 sted by: Counseling and Psychological Services (CAPS)\, Neal-Marshall Bla
 ck Culture Center\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https://bein
 volved.indiana.edu/event/12871490
DTEND:20261023T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20261010T053119Z
DTSTART:20261022T223000Z
GEO:39.168410;-86.516700
LOCATION:Bridgwaters Lounge
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Twice as Hard: Booked\, Busy\, and Burnt Out
UID:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12871490
URL:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12871490
X-HOSTS:Neal-Marshall Black Culture Center
END:VEVENT
